 "notes": [
  "There is no keyword/full-text search. BBC's robots.txt disallows /search, so find content through section, region and topic listings, list-live-pages, or search-football-teams.",
  "Listing commands return relative hrefs such as /news/articles/{id}, /news/videos/{id} and /news/live/{id}. The last path segment is the id that get-article, get-video and get-live-blog take. The same story can appear more than once on a listing page.",
  "get-article returns schema.org metadata only (headline, description, author, dates, image), not the full body text. The body is in the page's script#__NEXT_DATA__.",
  "Pagination on section and region pages is client-side only. Only topic pages (?page=N) have real paginated URLs.",
  "Football: use search-football-teams to get a team slug (from the result url /sport/football/teams/{slug}/scores-fixtures), then call list-team-fixtures.",
  "Content is geo-dependent: the recording came from a US IP, and some UK-only content may differ.",
  "Saving articles needs a signed-in BBC account. No save endpoint was captured (the explorer was not logged in), so writes are not supported."
